Here's how to implement all three requirements:

## 1. Custom "Cancel" Back Button

In your `EditProductPage.xaml`:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.EditProductPage"
             Shell.BackButtonBehavior="{StaticResource CancelBackButton}">

    <ContentPage.Resources>
        <BackButtonBehavior x:Key="CancelBackButton"
                            TextOverride="Cancel"
                            Command="{Binding BackCommand}" />
    </ContentPage.Resources>

    <!-- your form here -->
</ContentPage>
```

## 2. Intercept Hardware/Gesture Back Navigation

Override `OnBackButtonPressed` in your code-behind:

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    public EditProductPage()
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        BindingContext = new EditProductViewModel();
    }

    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (BindingContext is EditProductViewModel vm && vm.HasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            // Fire-and-forget the async dialog; return true to cancel navigation
            MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(async () =>
            {
                bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                    "Unsaved Changes",
                    "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                    "Discard", "Stay");

                if (leave)
                    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
            });

            return true; // cancel the default back navigation
        }

        return base.OnBackButtonPressed();
    }
}
```

## 3. ViewModel with BackCommand

```csharp
public class EditProductViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged
{
    public bool HasUnsavedChanges { get; set; }

    public ICommand BackCommand { get; }

    public EditProductViewModel()
    {
        BackCommand = new Command(async () =>
        {
            if (HasUnsavedChanges)
            {
                bool leave = await Shell.Current.CurrentPage.DisplayAlert(
                    "Unsaved Changes",
                    "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                    "Discard", "Stay");

                if (!leave) return;
            }

            await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
        });
    }

    // INotifyPropertyChanged implementation...
}
```

**Key points:**

- **`BackButtonBehavior`** replaces the back arrow with a "Cancel" text button and routes taps through your `BackCommand`.
- **`OnBackButtonPressed`** catches the Android hardware back button / swipe gesture. Return `true` to cancel navigation, then conditionally call `GoToAsync("..")`.
- Both paths share the same confirmation logic — the dialog only appears when `HasUnsavedChanges` is `true`.

> ⚠️ **iOS swipe-back gesture** isn't caught by `OnBackButtonPressed`. To fully block it, disable it via the platform-specific `Shell.PrefersLargeTitles` or set `IsEnabled="false"` on the `BackButtonBehavior` when there are unsaved changes, which disables the gesture on iOS.
